<p class="lt-chem-38252">Find the boiling point of a solution of 92.1 g of iodine, \(\ce{I2}\), in 800.0 g of chloroform, \(\ce{CHCl3}\), assuming that the iodine is nonvolatile and that the solution is ideal.</p>

<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Chemistry_1e_(OpenSTAX)/11:_Solutions_and_Colloids/11.05:_Colligative_Properties" class="mt-section"><span id="Solution_5"></span><h6 id="Solution-38252"><span>Solution</span></h6>

<p class="lt-chem-38252">We can solve this problem using four steps.</p>

<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-38252"><img alt="11.4.2.png" style="width: 806px; height: 143px;" width="806px" height="143px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/163386/11.4.2.png?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=806&amp;height=143" /></p>

